<title>UK: BSkyB tumbles after U.S. selling overnight.</title>
<headline>BSkyB tumbles after U.S. selling overnight.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in BSkyB were marked down 14-1/2p to 514-1/2p in pre-market dealings on the back of heavy selling in the U.S. overnight, traders said.  </p>
<p>The ADRs lost 3-1/8 to 50-5/8 in New York.</p>
<p>Traders linked the selling pressure to perceptions there was an overhang of shares on the back of News Corp's recent issue.</p>
<p>BSkyB shares, down to their lowest level since mid-August, have fallen by about 25 percent from their October 18 peak.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
